  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "P.Tejraj vs The Food Safety Officer on 19 February, 2025",
    "facts": "2. The case of the prosecution is that on 28.06.2019, the complainant gone to Mahavir Nuts & Spices at No.32/32 Theosophical Society, Near Raja Veedi, Coimbatore with an intention to take food samples and at that time the petitioner/A-1 was selling the food items in his shop to general public. The complainant had enquired about Boiled Papaya Cubes in Sugar to the first accused and the complainant had purchased 1kg packets (Nos. 60) from the petitioner/A-1 and had taken samples of the said product and sealed the same in accordance with the procedure as contemplated under the Food Safety and Standards ACt 2006 and had sent the same to the Food analyst on 01.07.2019. 1 food analyst had tested the product from 01.07.2019 to 31.01.2020 and the food analyst had sent a report on 05.02.2020 stating that the sample had added color exceed the defined limit as unsafe. The report was sent to the petitioner/A-1 and the designated officer had sent a letter rejecting the appeal stating that the product had already lost its expiry. The complainant had sought for permission to file a case against the accused to the designated officer and the same was granted by the commissioner of Food Safety and hence, he has filed the above complaint before the Judicial Magistrate No.V Coimbatore under the provisions of Section 59 (i) of Food Safety and Standards https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis Act, 2006 and 190(1)(A) and 200 C.P.C. Hence, the petitioner filed this petition to quash the proceedings in S.T.C No. 5175 of 2020 pending on the file of the Judicial Magistrate No.V, Coimbatore. Therefore, the petitioner was not able send the food sample to referral laboratory owing to the delay on the part of the complainant/respondent.",
    "arguments": "3. The learned counsel for the petitioner submits that as per Section 42 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006, Food analyst ought to have analysed the sample and send the analysis report within 14 days to the designated officer.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "3. The learned counsel for the petitioner submits that as per Section 42 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006, Food analyst ought to have analysed the sample and send the analysis report within 14 days to the designated officer.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
